    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Josh Naylor** (66.42) and **James Wood** (60.25) leading the offensive charge. **Josh Naylor** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Burke, S, providing a high-floor profile as a cleanup hitter, while **James Wood**\u2019s leadoff spot provides the highest order-advantage boost (+10%) in our lineup. **Seiya Suzuki** (60.04) also registers as a strong start; despite a tough matchup against Rocker, his ability to exploit a slow delivery from the mound\u2014making him a prime candidate for a stolen base\u2014pushes him over the 60.0 threshold. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) remains our most statistically secure play, bolstered by an 11% skill-advantage boost against Montero, making him the anchor of our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who finished just shy of the lineup at 41.62. While his raw metrics were competitive, the optimizer penalized his assumed #9 spot and a significant platoon disadvantage (-13%), prioritizing the safer floor provided by **Cole Young** in the middle infield. We are also closely monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Seiya Suzuki**, as their scores are contingent on pending lineup confirmation; should their spots shift lower in the order, their efficiency scores will inevitably fluctuate. **Tyler Soderstrom** offers a high-variance upside today, with a 16% park-factor adjustment masking the difficulty of facing a pitcher of Bradish\u2019s caliber. We are avoiding the sub-40 floor of **Travis Bazzana** and **Kyle Karros**, as the volatility of their respective matchups against Prielipp and Luzardo makes them inefficient use of our game caps for this rotation.",
